# Tor config tuned for SuperStress monerod P2P-over-Tor.
#
# The stressnet has ~3 live nodes, all on port 28080, which most Tor exits
# reject. Two defaults make reconnects brutal for this workload:
#   - SocksTimeout 120: a connect attempt through a bad path can hang a
#     connection slot for 2 minutes before failing.
#   - MaxCircuitDirtiness 600: after 10 minutes, new streams get a fresh
#     circuit through a random exit that probably rejects 28080 again.
# So: fail fast, and stick to exits that are known to work.
SocksPort 0.0.0.0:9050
SocksPolicy accept 10.0.0.0/8
SocksPolicy accept 172.16.0.0/12
SocksPolicy accept 192.168.0.0/16
SocksPolicy reject *

# Fail bad paths in 15s instead of 120s so monerod's retry loop cycles fast.
SocksTimeout 15

# Keep reusing a working circuit (and its 28080-friendly exit) for 24h
# instead of rotating every 10 minutes. Slightly weaker unlinkability,
# acceptable for a public stressnet node whose only secret is its IP.
MaxCircuitDirtiness 86400

DataDirectory /var/lib/tor
Log notice stdout
